# Draft knowledge entry — strict-variant 0.5 source-root selection

id:                     DRAFT-strict-variant-0.5-nested-source-selection
trigger_tool:           init-build|conan|cmake
phase:                  initialization|packaging|testing
error_signature:        first nested CMakeLists.txt|bench/eggs-variant|wrong source root|strict_variant headers missing
severity:               2
category:               build-system, packaging, header-only, testing
match_keywords:         strict-variant, header-only, top-level include, nested CMake, benchmark, source-root selection, init-build, expected SKIP, upstream inventory
title:                  Anchor header-only package layout to the top-level public tree before selecting nested build projects

root_cause:             Some source archives contain a valid top-level public header tree and test tree plus unrelated nested examples or benchmarks. A first-match recursive build-file detector can select the nested benchmark as the source root, causing the recipe to package the wrong headers or report the wrong build system even though the requested library is present at the archive root.
affected_scope:         Header-only C/C++ archives with top-level include/ and test/ directories and unrelated nested CMakeLists.txt, Makefile, or other build markers.
verification_cmd:       Inspect the archive inventory, identify the public include/<library>/ tree and upstream test entry before accepting an automatically promoted nested source root; then build and run the source-keyed upstream inventory plus a real consumer.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           top-level-public-tree-anchor
rec_description:        Prefer a top-level public include tree and its declared upstream test entry when they exist. Treat nested CMake projects as candidates only after proving that their targets consume the requested library tree. Preserve the complete upstream inventory and separate executed PASS from expected conditional SKIP.
rec_command:            find <source> -maxdepth 2 -type d -name include -o -name test; rg -n "project\(|add_executable|strict_variant" <source>
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-explicit-source-root

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      manual-source-root-audit
fallback_description:   If the detector chooses a nested project, compare its include paths and target names with the requested package before using it. Do not silently lift or delete sibling public/test directories.
fallback_command:       tar -tzf <archive> | rg "(^|/)include/strict_variant/|(^|/)test/|CMakeLists.txt"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          explicit-package-surface-and-test-manifest

forbid_1_pattern:       accept first nested CMakeLists.txt|package bench/eggs-variant as strict-variant|drop top-level include
forbid_1_reason:        A nested benchmark may be a different project and can produce a successful but unrelated build or an empty/wrong package.
forbid_1_consequence:   Consumers receive the wrong public API and upstream test evidence no longer describes the packaged library.
forbid_2_pattern:       report upstream total 0|count expected SKIP as PASS|remove skipped target from inventory
forbid_2_reason:        The source tree and its conditional test semantics remain part of the reviewable coverage contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   PR statistics hide real coverage and unsupported optional capability is misrepresented as a product pass.

principles:             real-source-inventory, public-surface-first, explicit-test-boundary, transparent-skip-counting
similar_to:             E195, E466, E413
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-strict-variant-0.5-nested-source-selection.md
last_updated:           2026-09-03
source_event:           strict-variant 0.5 OHOS PC adaptation: init-build selected bench/eggs-variant before the top-level header library
authors:                Awstme <awstme@qq.com>
source_pr:
source_commit:

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.84
metrics_last_used:      2026-09-03

